muros (0.9.64) trixie; urgency=medium

  * L2TP: the last PPP type still generated as an mpd5 configuration now runs
    under xl2tpd, with the pppd options file generated like the other types and a
    lac that dials on startup and redials for ever, supervised by a
    muros-l2tp@<interface>.service template. xl2tpd is a recommendation.
  * NetFlow local collection: flowd has no Debian package and both the collector
    and the aggregator were started through FreeBSD rc scripts, so nothing was
    ever collected and the Insight pages stayed empty. Only the daemon was
    missing: the reporting side reads the flowd log with the parser shipped in
    tree, so a collector receives the datagrams sent to the loopback, decodes
    NetFlow version 5 and version 9 including templates, and appends records in
    that same format. It keeps the flowd pid file contract so the aggregator can
    rotate the log and have it reopened. Both run as units, the collector shows
    up in the service list.

