muros (0.9.63) trixie; urgency=medium

  * PPTP: sessions run under pppd like PPPoE, with the pptp helper handed to
    pppd as its terminal, a default MTU accounting for the GRE and IP headers
    and EAP refused since a PPTP server offering it cannot be authenticated
    against. The unit template is now muros-ppp@ for both types and an interface
    reset stops either. pptp-linux is a recommendation.
  * Interfaces: the 6rd and 6to4 tunnels are sit tunnels created with iproute2,
    encapsulated in the WAN address and without a fixed remote, with the 6rd
    delegated prefix and relay prefix passed as tunnel attributes. They were
    stf(4) pseudo interfaces driven by ifconfig, so an interface in either mode
    stayed dark. That was the last ifconfig call of interfaces.inc.
  * Interfaces: the unreachable FreeBSD bodies of the PPP and wireless paths are
    removed, several hundred lines of mpd5 configuration, netgraph control
    messages and ifconfig radio settings that could never run.
  * Diagnostics: kernel memory usage is built from /proc/meminfo and
    /proc/slabinfo instead of vmstat with the FreeBSD libxo output.

