muros (0.9.58) trixie; urgency=medium

  * IPv6 WAN: finish the port. An interface in slaac mode was rendered with
    IPv6AcceptRA=no, so the kernel ignored the router advertisements and the
    interface never got an address, and interface_dhcpv6_configure() still
    started rtsold, which does not exist on Debian and was the only thing
    starting dhcp6c. Advertisements are now accepted on the link, the networkd
    units are re-rendered and the link reconfigured so the DHCPv6 client
    solicits immediately. The DHCPv6 options of the interface (prefix delegation
    hint, resolver request) are rendered into the unit.
  * IPv6 WAN: the lease handler also diffs the dynamic IPv6 addresses and the
    default router of each device, publishes the router through ifctl and
    replays the newipv6 chain. Advertisements leave no file to watch, so a
    periodic sweep was added next to the DHCPv4 path unit.
  * Interfaces: speed and duplex are read and forced with ethtool instead of
    ifconfig media. The details parser reported no media at all, so the settings
    page offered an empty list and hid the field, and the enforcement code read
    an undefined value. Values migrated from a FreeBSD configuration are
    normalised. ethtool is now a dependency.

