    to start and high availability never came up. MurOS owns the full Kea
    state, so the profiles are disabled the same way the unbound profile
    already is. Validated by loading a MurOS-style hot-standby HA configuration
    (both hook libraries) through "kea-dhcp4 -t" on Debian 13.

